# deploy/host/ufw/policy — the default policies of the main server's UFW
# (docs/host-state.md#the-firewall-ufw). scripts/vpn-bot-ufw-apply sets them.
#
#   role|direction|policy      direction: incoming | outgoing; policy: allow | deny | reject
#
# Seeded from the main server as measured on 2026-11-12 (/etc/default/ufw:
# DEFAULT_INPUT_POLICY="DROP", DEFAULT_OUTPUT_POLICY="ACCEPT").
#
# The routed policy is NOT here and is never changed: AWG clients and WARP reach the
# internet through route rules (the module table of vpn-bot-ufw-apply), and the
# measured DEFAULT_FORWARD_POLICY="DROP" stays exactly as the host has it.
#
# A change of the incoming policy (and enabling an inactive ufw) runs under a dead-man:
# it stays only with a proof that ssh still answers from outside — a new connection
# in the sshd log, or «Подтвердить» in the bot — else it is reverted after 10 minutes.
main|incoming|deny
main|outgoing|allow
